        fp: "A wealthy philanthropist orally promised the board of trustees of a non-profit private university that he would donate $5,000,000 to construct a new state-of-the-art biological sciences research laboratory[cite: 39]. In direct and foreseeable reliance on the philanthropist's oral pledge, the university hired an architectural firm to draft $150,000 in architectural blueprints, paid $100,000 in non-refundable permitting fees to the city, and broke ground on foundation excavation[cite: 39]. Six months later, following a dispute with the university president over faculty hiring policies, the philanthropist repudiated his pledge and refused to transfer any funds[cite: 39]. The university sued the philanthropist to enforce the $5,000,000 charitable pledge[cite: 39].",
